blish local exposure, assistance, harvests, displacement, or market supply in Namentenga."}], "actions": [{"action": "Maintain district-level market-price and availability monitoring and pre-position contingency support such as targeted cash or staple assistance if local affordability deteriorates.", "urgency": "prepare_now", "driver_channels": ["wfp_staple_price", "wfp_staple_price_change_1m_pct", "wfp_staple_price_change_3m_pct"], "justification": "Country-level maize prices remained above their January level and retained positive three-month increases through June. Local monitoring is needed because the available price evidence is not district-specific."}, {"action": "Prepare conflict-sensitive access and referral arrangements with local partners, including contingency plans for households whose movement to markets or services is interrupted.", "urgency": "prepare_now", "driver_channels": ["acled_events", "acled_events_sum_3m", "acled_fatalities", "last_available_phase"], "justification": "National conflict activity persisted and fatalities were elevated in May, while the latest June assessment at cutoff was Phase 3. This recommendation addresses a plausible access risk rather than asserting that national conflict caused district food insecurity."}]}

